      "formal_name": "lt_add_one",
      "informal_name": "Strict inequality under adding one: $a < a + 1$",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "type": "∀ {α : Type u_1} [inst : One α] [inst_1 : AddZeroClass α] [inst_2 : PartialOrder α] [ZeroLEOneClass α] [NeZero 1]\n  [AddLeftStrictMono α] (a : α), a < a + 1",
      "informal_description": "Let $\\alpha$ be a type with a partial order, equipped with a zero element, a one element, and an addition operation such that:\n1. $0 \\leq 1$ (ZeroLEOneClass)\n2. $1 \\neq 0$ (NeZero)\n3. Addition is strictly monotone on the left (AddLeftStrictMono)\n\nThen for any element $a \\in \\alpha$, we have $a < a + 1$.",
